+## Upgrading to 1.0.1 {#upgrade-101}
+
+Install matching 1.0.1 library and SQL files on the primary and replicas, restart each server to reload the preloaded library, then run `ALTER EXTENSION pg_tokenizer UPDATE TO '1.0.1';` in each primary database. Paths from 0.1.0, 0.1.1 and 1.0.0 preserve signatures, vocabulary IDs and stored data. The new standby cache signal becomes active only after this SQL change commits and replays.
+
+Qualify missing/ambiguous legacy pg_dict references before upgrading; explicitly qualify custom dictionaries that deliberately shadow builtin names. Review the [new resource budgets](/docs/tokenizer/reference/#definition-caches) for bulk ingestion. The runtime schema layout remains unchanged: database owners still need CREATE on tokenizer_catalog for vocabulary tables. The new counter grants PUBLIC only SELECT; its internal trigger is SECURITY DEFINER with a fixed search_path and no public EXECUTE grant.
