+Since 1.0.1, creation resolves the name and stores its schema-qualified form. Later calls use that name independently of the session search_path and resolve its OID once per batch, so DROP/CREATE and ALTER no longer require reconnecting. Renaming/moving the dictionary requires updating the analyzer. Upgrade pins old builtin names to pg_catalog and unique custom names to their schema; ambiguous or missing names must be qualified before upgrade. Changes to external dictionary files still follow PostgreSQL's normal reload rules.
